INT. TWENTY-SECOND FLOOR CONFERENCE ROOM, SYNERGEX CORP - DAY

A glass-walled room with a view of a parking structure the CEO insists on calling "the skyline." A laminated sign reads: THIS IS A SAFE SPACE FOR RADICAL CANDOR.

CHIP HALLORAN-TSENG (40s, quarter-zip, laser pointer) presides at the head of the table. Beside him, a flip chart with a single word on it: SYNERGY. Around the table sit DAHLIA OKORO (30s, analyst, perfect posture), BERNARD "BUZZ" KOWALSKI (50s, thirty years in accounting, cardigan) and PRIYA NANDAKUMAR (20s, intern, notebook open to a blank page).

Chip circles the room, laser dot dancing across the ceiling tile. Dahlia writes a note and crosses it out. Buzz unwraps a butterscotch. Priya's pen hovers over her notebook.

CHIP
Okay, team. Radical candor. Dahlia, what's one thing you'd change about how we work?

DAHLIA
Honestly, Chip? Meetings.

CHIP
Love that. Candid. Buzz?

BUZZ
Meetings.

CHIP
We're hearing a lot of meetings. Priya, you're new, fresh eyes.

PRIYA
Um. I don't know. Maybe the meetings?

CHIP
(to the flip chart)
Okay. So the through-line, and I want to be sensitive here, is some of you feel there may be a perception of too many meetings.

Buzz stands, walks to the window, and stares at the parking structure. Dahlia takes the laser pointer from Chip's hand while he is mid-gesture and sets it on the table. Priya's pen has started to write, small, tight letters. Chip blinks at his empty hand.

DAHLIA
Chip, we've had this meeting four times.

CHIP
Dahlia, I appreciate that, and I'm going to park that.

BUZZ
(from the window)
Park it where? There's no parking. It's a parking structure and there is no parking.

CHIP
Buzz.

BUZZ
I have been here thirty years, Chip. I have given you eleven reports on how to fix the parking. You have given me a mug.

CHIP
We value you.

BUZZ
It has a motivational otter on it.

PRIYA
(small)
I like the otter.

Everyone looks at her. She shrinks, then, to her own surprise, does not.

PRIYA (CONT'D)
But I also think this meeting is eating the whole day and nobody's doing the work. Sorry. Radical candor.

Silence. Chip lifts the cap off a marker, caps it, uncaps it. Dahlia leans back. Buzz turns from the window with his arms folded and a look of dawning joy.

BUZZ
Chip, she's right.

CHIP
Priya, I hear you, and the thing with candor--

DAHLIA
Chip.

CHIP
--is it needs a framework--

BUZZ
(at once)
Chip.

CHIP
(louder)
--and a safe space!

He slaps the flip chart. It topples. SYNERGY lands face-down on the carpet. Priya, Buzz and Dahlia look at it, then at him. He looks at it too. He straightens his quarter-zip.

CHIP (CONT'D)
Let's circle back.

Dahlia stands. Buzz unwraps another butterscotch and offers Priya one. She takes it. They file out in a line, and Chip is left alone with the otter mug and a view of the garage.
